cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the article and this software archive."
title: "Replication package: Calibrating Point-Optimal Unit Root Tests for Level Breaks in Small Samples: Evidence from Real Exchange Rates"
abstract: >-
  Code, data and result files that reproduce the article and its online supplement
  section by section (one script per section, python replicate_sec_4.py for
  example, with a quick mode and a full mode that regenerates every simulation from
  the recorded seeds), and a standalone command that applies the paper's Model LB
  unit root test with known level breaks to a user's own series
  (python -m model_lb).
authors:
  - family-names: "Gonçalves Silva"
    given-names: "Ricardo"
    email: "ricardogs@alumni.usp.br"
version: 3.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ricardogs-econ/model-LB-replication"
keywords:
  - "unit root tests"
  - "level breaks"
  - "point-optimal tests"
  - "GLS detrending"
  - "finite-sample calibration"
  - "half-power point"
  - "real exchange rates"
  - "purchasing power parity"
  - "half-life"
  - "Monte Carlo"
